{
  "slug": "kubernetes-exec",
  "title": "exec",
  "content": [
    {
      "id": "kubernetes-exec",
      "title": "exec",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lead",
          "content": "<code>kubectl exec</code> runs a command, or opens an interactive shell, inside an already-running Pod."
        },
        {
          "type": "divider"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading1",
          "content": "1. Running Inside a Live Pod",
          "text": "1. Running Inside a Live Pod"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "<code>exec</code> reaches into a Pod that is already running and executes a command there directly, the Kubernetes-level equivalent of <code>docker exec</code>, covered throughout the Docker course."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "url": "https://algorithmxlr8-assets-images.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/devops-content-images/1784528378787-519460005.png",
          "content": "https://algorithmxlr8-assets-images.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/devops-content-images/1784528378787-519460005.png",
          "alt": "Reaching directly into a Pod that is already alive and running",
          "size": "medium"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "content": "kubectl exec my-app-7d9f8c-x2k4p -- ls /app",
          "code": {
            "language": "bash",
            "content": "kubectl exec my-app-7d9f8c-x2k4p -- ls /app"
          },
          "codes": {
            "bash": "kubectl exec my-app-7d9f8c-x2k4p -- ls /app"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "divider"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading1",
          "content": "2. The Interactive Form",
          "text": "2. The Interactive Form"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Adding <code>-it</code> gives you a full interactive session, most commonly a shell, the standard way to actually poke around inside a container live."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "url": "https://algorithmxlr8-assets-images.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/devops-content-images/1784528382908-63109900.png",
          "content": "https://algorithmxlr8-assets-images.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/devops-content-images/1784528382908-63109900.png",
          "alt": "A full interactive session, the standard way to explore a container live",
          "size": "medium"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "content": "kubectl exec -it my-app-7d9f8c-x2k4p -- bash",
          "code": {
            "language": "bash",
            "content": "kubectl exec -it my-app-7d9f8c-x2k4p -- bash"
          },
          "codes": {
            "bash": "kubectl exec -it my-app-7d9f8c-x2k4p -- bash"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "divider"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading1",
          "content": "3. Where the Deeper Context Lives",
          "text": "3. Where the Deeper Context Lives"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "This is a brief command reference, the full debugging context, including what to do when there is no shell available at all, is covered fully in the Observability module's dedicated topic."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "url": "https://algorithmxlr8-assets-images.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/devops-content-images/1784528388788-957410500.png",
          "content": "https://algorithmxlr8-assets-images.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/devops-content-images/1784528388788-957410500.png",
          "alt": "The reference here, the full debugging context in the Observability module",
          "size": "medium"
        },
        {
          "type": "final-thoughts",
          "title": "Key Takeaway",
          "points": [
            "kubectl exec runs a command, or an interactive shell with -it, inside an already-running Pod, the Kubernetes-level equivalent of docker exec.",
            "The Observability module covers the full debugging context this command is used within, including the no-shell case."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
